                         IRSAVE Read Me File
                          Beta Version 0.1
                             2/ 7/1997

==============================================================================
NOTE: The shareware version of IRSAVE is limited to saving files of less than
      2000 bytes. Larger files will be received but not saved. This way
      you can verify that the IR link works with your size files and
      equipment before you register for the full version. However, this version
      will create the directory structure necessary to recieve the file.
===============================================================================

What does IRSAVE do?
  IRSAVE allows you to receive files directly from your Siena or 3c using the
  native Psion IR protocol and IR Send key on the keyboard. No additional
  software is required on your Psion. Just follow the directions in your
  Psion manual for sending files to another Psion. The IRSAVE.COM program
  allows your PC to understand the Psion protocol. Files are saved in the same
  relative directory as on the Psion. But the files are saved with the current
  date and time on your PC (limitation of Psion protocol).

What doesn't IRSAVE do?
  IRSAVE does not handle receiving single records of a file or highlighted
  text. Only complete files.

How is the data protected?
  Each data block transferred is protected by a 16 bit CRC check code
  (x^0+x^5+x^12+x^16) and a 3 bit sequence number. Bad and missing blocks are
  automatically resent until received correctly by the PC. (per IRDA spec)

Can I send more than one file at a time?
  No. Only a highlighted file can be sent not 'tagged' files. However the PC
  program continues to loop waiting for more files so just keep highlighting
  and pressing the send key.

What baud rate is used to send the files?
  The initial negotiations start at 9600 baud per the IRDA spec and then
  go to 19,200 for the actual header and file transfer. If people experience
  problems during the 19,200 phase I may produce a second version of IRSAVE
  that just stays at 9600 baud.

What IR hardware works with IRSAVE?
   Well, that's the purpose of this beta. You tell me and then I can post
   the results and/or try to fix the problems.

   I have not had much luck with external units since they need to be setup for
   the baud rate and IRSAVE does not do that yet. A single baud rate IRSAVE
   might get around that limitation for now.

Where can I get the latest version?
   A web site has been setup at:

       http://www.geocities.com/SiliconValley/Lakes/3947

   It has the latest version of IRSAVE plus access to other Psion IR programs
   and information about current and future plans.

IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT  IMPORTANT
==============================================================================
It is highly recommended that you verify the accuracy of a few large files
after doing your first IRSAVE. If you have text files, open an editor and view
the file, checking the beginning and end for correctness. If you have a binary
compare program try comparing the copied version of a program with a
known good copy (one you previously loaded into your PSION from your PC).
