==============================================================================

Requirements:
  PSION: Siena or 3c
  PC   : x86 with IRDA compliant IR port
  Operating System: DOS, Windows 3.1, OS/2 2.1, OS/2 Warp 3,
                    WIN95 (MS-DOS mode only)

Files in this package:
  IRSAVE.COM      Program that receives files from your Psion.
  README.SAV      This file.

Installation:
  Load IRSAVE.COM on your PC.

Running IRSAVE.
  Be sure to set the IR Link to run at HIGH power. From the system screen press
  Psion-L select Infrared then Power setting to HIGH. Then just type IRSAVE
  followed by the COM number for your IR port. IRSAVE continues to loop
  receiving files from your Psion until you terminate the program by holding
  down both shift keys on the PC.

    Files received are save in the same relative path as on your Psion.
  However they will have the current date and time not the date and time of
  the original file on your Psion. Sorry, the Psion native protocol does not
  include this information.

  Syntax of IRSAVE.COM:

             irsave <IR port> </t>

    Examples:
      irsave 2      (Use COM port 2 to receive files)
      irsave 1 /t   (Use COM port 1 and display link activity, used for debug)

Aborting the program:
  To abort IRSAVE on the PC just hold down both the left and right shift
  keys for a few seconds.

Improvements:
  If you have any suggestions for improvements please email me with them.

Registration:
  If you find this program useful please register your copy. Registered users
  will receive the full version that supports receiving any size file.

  Currently registration is only through the mail. Mail $10 (US currency only
